          "en": "<p>Following the decline of the Western Roman Empire and the banning of gladiatorial games in the 5th and 6th centuries, the Colosseum fell into neglect. Powerful medieval Roman families like the Frangipani turned the ruined monument into a fortified castle.</p><p>Devastating earthquakes in 847 and 1349 toppled its outer southern wall. For centuries, the ruins served as a free marble quarry: popes and princes looted tens of thousands of tons of travertine blocks and bronze clamps to construct palaces and St. Peter's Basilica.</p>",
